      'Opening deal: 2-6 player(s), 5 card(s) per player, 1 deck(s), initial visibility face_down.',
      'Opening flow: start in play; each_player_clockwise may use play_card before round end.',
      'Scoring check: Melded cards score points: aces and wild cards are typically worth 100 points each (or 200 when aces are wild); other picture cards and tens are 10 points; numeral cards 2–9 are 5 points. Unmelded cards left in hand at the end of a hand count against the player, and going out may award a bonus. Target score is often 5000, but many groups use 1500, 2000, 2200, 2500, 2800 or 10000. Expected outcome: Be the first player to reach the target score (often 5000) by melding sets and runs and going out; opponents add deadwood to your score..',
